<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the Second Coalition</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1798">1798</a>–<a href="/years/1802">1802</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-wars">French Revolutionary Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the Second Coalition was fought between Revolutionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and an alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and others. After early coalition successes in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> in 1799, including the battles around Zürich, France under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a> won at Marengo and Hohenlinden in 1800. The treaties of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luneville">Lunéville</a> in 1801 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amiens">Amiens</a> in 1802 ended the war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-second-coalition.jpg" alt="War of the Second Coalition" width="320" height="360" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ruedi33a · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:War_of_the_second_coalition.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
